@startuml
title M-SH1 - Process ownership: current / SH1 and gated SH2+
left to right direction

package "Current / SH1 extraction (no behaviour change)" {
  node "Operator user account" as current_user {
    component "task-board client / producers" as current_board
    component "tb-sessiond\nboard executable + composition root\none daemon per BoardKey" as daemon
    component "Claude Code\nPTY master held by tb-sessiond" as current_claude
    component "Codex private app-server\none per session" as current_codex
    database "User state directory\nboard-keyed host records / transcripts\nper-session notice inbox" as current_state
  }
  current_board --> daemon : compatibility seam / bearer token
  current_board --> current_state : direct notice writes
  daemon --> current_claude : owns PTY master
  daemon --> current_codex : owns private app-server
  daemon --> current_state : host state
  note bottom of daemon
    SH1 supplies a serving library; executable stays in board through C1.
    Claude dies on daemon replacement; startup is self-restoring.
    Muse PTY factory registered in production; MSP factory unregistered.
    Hosted launch decodes input, then refuses capability admission.
    Recovery details beyond these facts: unspecified in spec §1.1.
  end note
}

package "SH2+ target - disabled until joint activation gates" {
  node "Orchestrator account or service account" {
    component "Optional board client" as board
    database "Board goal ledger / run evidence\nowner: board" as board_state
  }
  component "Launching caller / launcher\ninitial goal author" as caller
  component "agent-session-bridge\ncarrier / Mailbox" as bridge
  database "Durable mail\nowner: bridge" as mail
  node "swarma-session-host service account" {
    component "swarma-session-host\ncontroller / input admission" as host
    database "Metadata, logs, transcripts, receipts\nfences, controller epochs, goal revisions\nowner: host" as host_state
  }
  component "swarma-dispatcher\nUnix-socket service from first slice\nadmission / allocation / execution / cleanup" as dispatcher
  database "Admission, allocation, execution records\nsession-scoped host admission permit\nowner: dispatcher" as dispatch_state
  component "swarma-user-manager\nowned generation / exec.stop" as manager
  database "Root-owned active-generation ledger\nowner: user manager" as ledger
  node "User-manager module / root launch boundary" {
    component "swarma-user-launcher" as root_launcher
  }
  node "worker-<label> trusted-class local placement - one runner per session" {
    component "swarma-session-runner\nPTY master or app-server transport\ncredential lease client" as runner
    component "Claude Code\nor qualified provider harness" as harness
    component "Codex private app-server\nno shared pool" as appserver
  }
  component "swarma-credential-broker\nCodex auth owner refreshes account" as broker

  board --> board_state : board facts / optional completion barrier
  board --> host : authenticated optional goal client
  caller --> dispatcher : owner-admitted start; optional session lifecycle authorisation
  caller --> host : authorised goal client (§3.8)
  bridge --> mail : durable receipt of mail
  bridge --> host : enqueue; count delivery after durable write
  host --> host_state : durable write before acknowledgement
  host --> dispatcher : host_start / host_stop (dispatch-op/1)
  dispatcher --> dispatch_state : admission and cleanup ownership
  dispatcher --> host : admission / effect / receipt evidence
  dispatcher --> manager : exec.stop
  dispatcher --> root_launcher : sole privileged start caller; claim / effect / root receipt
  manager --> ledger : owned active generation
  manager --> root_launcher : module's privileged launcher
  root_launcher --> runner : receipt before UID/GID change and exec\nFD3 plan only; no broker descriptor
  runner <--> host : authenticated reconnect / readiness / current epoch input
  runner --> harness : start only admitted harness / owns PTY master
  runner --> appserver : admitted private app-server / owns transport
  runner --> broker : open after UID change; lease renewals

  note bottom of host
    Refuse stale epoch, invalid capability, legacy global token,
    unreadable / malformed / retired identity and unsupported starters.
    Closed fence queues within byte/count budgets without delivery; unknown readiness parks.
    Reserve / charge producer and aggregate retained bytes before durable acceptance.
    Debt survives replacement / retirement; producer cannot consume control/evidence reserve.
    Bounded runner buffers / dispatcher output handoff; backpressure / refusal or park / host_stop.
    Admission needs reserve; incomplete evidence remains closed / unknown (§7.20).
    Unchanged principal/id claim compares complete canonical signed intent via envelope_digest.
    Exact retry returns original receipt; changed intent conflicts / new ID required (§7.19).
    Host loop: trusted class + local placement + admitted launch, never circle alone.
    Controller failure: reconcile before input; live runner may be
    re-adopted with same execution ID. Replacement requires confirmed absence.
    Trusted standing sessions / executions have no preset lifetime or runtime limit.
    Only explicit stop, operator action or own exit ends the session (§3.5).
    Park and restart preserve it; dispatcher runtime maximum is non-standing only.
    Durable intent and closed fence precede host_start.
    Session-scoped permit: logical_session_id; owner session lifecycle authorisation.
    Each start keeps execution_id / controller_epoch / op_id claim and fence.
    Fence change withdraws affected start authority or requires reconciliation.
    Host failure retains dispatcher claim and closed fence.
    R-MAINT: dispatcher bounded maintenance stop; deadline bounds attempt.
    Unknown/refused stop defers maintenance; absence and reconciliation
    precede mode/state/binary changes. Keep standing allocations / identities;
    after R-MAINT, fresh owner admission; no live supervisor adoption or automatic expiry.
  end note
  note bottom of root_launcher
    Dispatcher starts approved runner through existing claim / effect / root receipt.
    Cancel before call prevents call; ambiguity resolves same effect / receipt.
    Stop if required; never launch twice (R-START, §3.3).
    Approved executor path/digest, generation and home checked;
    environment and descriptors reset, atomic start receipt written,
    then groups cleared and GID/UID set.
    Runner opens fresh authenticated host channel after UID change.
    Current-epoch registration and readiness precede delivery.
    Channel / proof formats: unpublished (§7); FD3 plan only.
  end note
  note bottom of broker
    Board runner / host ask dispatcher; they embed no broker client.
    Agent-side curator-run is the first broker consumer and shares
    a launch library with the runner; it executes an immutable caller plan.
    Renewal timeout fails the turn; no native-auth fallback.
    Broker durable layout and external service UIDs: unspecified in spec §3.2.
  end note
  note bottom of manager
    Dispatcher v0 refuses interactive / resume.
    User-manager v0/v1: dispatcher-to-root caller/role policy.
    Caller-bound signed grants: v2 activation gate, grammar unpublished.
    exec.stop proves process absence only; unknown evidence holds capacity.
  end note
  note bottom of runner
    On restart, fresh runner checks native-lock absence under agent account
    and closed host fence before harness initialisation / resume;
    reports to host. Unknown result keeps session parked (§3.5).
    Agent has no goal capability; proposal must not mutate a goal (D-GOALS).
  end note
}

note bottom of dispatcher
  Ownership and qualification: spec §§3.1-3.5, 3.7; unpublished formats: §7.
  Web default-off; trusted-circle opt-in only; read-only task resources (§3.1).
end note
